			(property "Description" "Cortex Debug Connector, standard ARM Cortex-M SWD and JTAG interface -- real, common 2x5 1.27mm-pitch header (ARM CoreSight 10-pin 'Cortex Debug' connector, e.g. as used on Segger J-Link / ST-Link / Black Magic Probe adapters). Chosen for the Fanstel BT840's SWD programming/debug: this module's SWDIO (pin 16) and SWDCLK (pin 15) are already placed as U3 on connectivity.kicad_sch (see programming_debug_notes in regulation_notes.md / README for the cross-sheet pin reference -- not re-placing U3 here per task constraints). P0.18/RESET (U3 pin 14) maps to this connector's pin 10 (~RESET); module GND (U3 pins 10/A0/B0/C0/D0/F0/F1/F2/F3) maps to pins 3/5/9 here. VTref (pin 1) should be tied to the regulated +3V3 rail (see regulation.kicad_sch) once wiring is added, so debug-probe level-shifters reference the correct I/O voltage. SWO/TDO (pin 6) can optionally pick up an SWO/TRACE-capable GPIO for trace output; the pin is not yet allocated. JTAG-only pins (NC/TDI, KEY) are not used by the BT840 (SWD-only debug, per the nRF52840 inside it) and stay unconnected by design, matching this connector's own standard 'SWD-only subset' usage pattern."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
				)
			)
